{"name":"Fingerprint","hex":"#555356","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"fingerprint","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The natural pattern of ridges on the tips of human fingers, unique to each individual.","The pattern left on a surface where an uncovered fingertip has touched, especially as used to identify the person who touched the surface."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To take somebody's fingerprints.","To identify something uniquely by a combination of measurements."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fingerprint"}],"entries":[{"title":"Fingerprint","blocks":[{"text":"A fingerprint is an impression left by the friction ridges of a human finger. The recovery of partial fingerprints from a crime scene is an important method of forensic science. Moisture and grease on a finger result in fingerprints on surfaces such as glass or metal. Deliberate impressions of entire fingerprints can be obtained by ink or other substances transferred from the peaks of friction ridges on the skin to a smooth surface such as paper. Fingerprint records normally contain impressions from the pad on the last joint of fingers and thumbs, though fingerprint cards also typically record portions of lower joint areas of the fingers."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/10/Fingerprintforcriminologystubs.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fingerprint"},{"title":"Fingerprint (computing)","blocks":[{"text":"In computer science, a fingerprinting algorithm is a procedure that maps an arbitrarily large data item to a much shorter bit string, its fingerprint, that uniquely identifies the original data for all practical purposes just as human fingerprints uniquely identify people for practical purposes. This fingerprint may be used for data deduplication purposes. This is also referred to as file fingerprinting, data fingerprinting, or structured data fingerprinting."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fingerprint_(computing)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/78/Teerahertz_near-field_array_for_%CE%BCm-scale_surface_imaging_%28cropped%29.png/500px-Teerahertz_near-field_array_for_%CE%BCm-scale_surface_imaging_%28cropped%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/78/Teerahertz_near-field_array_for_%CE%BCm-scale_surface_imaging_%28cropped%29.png/500px-Teerahertz_near-field_array_for_%CE%BCm-scale_surface_imaging_%28cropped%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATeerahertz_near-field_array_for_%CE%BCm-scale_surface_imaging_(cropped).png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/Fingerprint_detail_on_male_finger_in_T%C5%99eb%C3%AD%C4%8D%2C_T%C5%99eb%C3%AD%C4%8D_District.jpg/500px-Fingerprint_detail_on_male_finger_in_T%C5%99eb%C3%AD%C4%8D%2C_T%C5%99eb%C3%AD%C4%8D_District.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/Fingerprint_detail_on_male_finger_in_T%C5%99eb%C3%AD%C4%8D%2C_T%C5%99eb%C3%AD%C4%8D_District.jpg/1280px-Fingerprint_detail_on_male_finger_in_T%C5%99eb%C3%AD%C4%8D%2C_T%C5%99eb%C3%AD%C4%8D_District.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/Fingerprint_detail_on_male_finger_in_T%C5%99eb%C3%AD%C4%8D%2C_T%C5%99eb%C3%AD%C4%8D_District.jpg/500px-Fingerprint_detail_on_male_finger_in_T%C5%99eb%C3%AD%C4%8D%2C_T%C5%99eb%C3%AD%C4%8D_District.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The friction ridges on a finger","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFingerprint_detail_on_male_finger_in_T%C5%99eb%C3%AD%C4%8D%2